# What gcloud uploads as the Cloud Build source tarball. Without this file
# gcloud derives the list from .gitignore, which keeps out .env and .venv
# but still ships artifacts/ and data/ -- adapters and Bethesda-derived
# dialogue that the build does not read and that need not sit in a staging
# bucket. Keep this in step with .dockerignore.
#
# Note the two files do different jobs: .gcloudignore decides what leaves
# the laptop, .dockerignore decides what the build daemon can COPY.
.git/
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/
artifacts/
data/
demo/
**/__pycache__/
*.log
.env
uv.lock
